  "yloVae273c_2": {
    "keep": true,
    "comment": "Finally, in line 154 of our work, by \"tighter bound\", we actually refer to a tighter dependence on the coverage ratio.\nFor example, in the tabular setting with $\\$ \\backslash$ Phi $\\$$ being the identity matrix, the term\n\n$$\n\\mu_1^{\\mathcal{B}}(x, a)^2\n$$\n\nacquires a factor of\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\mu_{\\mathcal{B}}(x, a)}\n$$\n\nin the summation, which can be large.\nThanks for noticing this; we will make our statement clearer in the final draft.",
    "reviewed_at": "2025-12-29T14:48:21.680657",
    "correct_formula_location": "LINE (154)"
  },
